(+1.0 s at 2000 m, +4.9 s at 2500 m, +11.6 s at 3500 m).                                                                
                                                                                                                        
In the repeat, ticks around distFromStart 2400-2700 show violent gear hunting: e.g. gear 6 -> 2 at ~100 km/h,           
then 3, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 2, 3, 2, 3, 4 within a few hundred metres, with brake only 0.2-0.3. Hypothesis: the              
braking downshift added in V3.2 uses an invented table _GEAR_SPEED_KMH_PER_1000RPM; the telemetry shows                 
6th gear at ~161 km/h is ~9300 rpm (about 17 km/h per 1000 rpm, not 44), so any light braking selects a                 
far too low gear, causing engine-braking spikes, wheel slip and steering corrections.                                   
                                                                                                                        
1. Confirm or refute with both ticks.csv files (count gear changes per lap in each run, and look at rpm vs              
   speedX per gear to estimate the real km/h per 1000 rpm for each gear 1-6).                                           
