   downshift ONE gear at a time, only when brake > 0.5 AND rpm < GEAR_DOWN_RPM_BRAKE (new PARAM, e.g. 5500),            
   never downshift if the resulting rpm would exceed GEAR_UP_RPM, and keep GEAR_HOLD_TICKS.                             
   Do not change any other parameter (corner speeds, braking, steering stay as V3.5).                                   
3. Add a self-test: at 100 km/h in 6th with brake 0.3 the gear must not drop below 5. Run the self-test.                
4. Add the analysis and V3.9 to CHANGELOG.md. Do not run the race or invent lap times.                                  

