Assistant (2) 2026-10-15 10:05:29.788 UTC (+423.3s)

The telemetry only partly supports your hypothesis. The gear table is wrong, but it isn't the whole story. I changed the
code, added the self-test (it passes) and wrote it all up in CHANGELOG.md. I did not run the race, so V3.9 has no lap   
time.                                                                                                                   
                                                                                                                        
1. Analysis (both ticks.csv, one lap each)                                                                              
                                                                                                                        
┌─────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────┬─────────────────┐                                              
│                                     │ 1:42.592 run   │ 1:55.606 repeat │                                              
├─────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┼─────────────────┤                                              
│ Gear changes (0–3600 m)             │ 152            │ 176             │                                              
├─────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┼─────────────────┤                                              
│ Downshifts                          │ 58             │ 57              │                                              
├─────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┼─────────────────┤                                              
│ Downshifts dropping 2 or more gears │ 28             │ 37              │                                              
├─────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┼─────────────────┤                                              
│ Downshifts at brake ≤ 0.3           │ 58 of 58       │ 51 of 57        │                                              
├─────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┼─────────────────┤                                              
│ Steering sign flips (|steer| > 0.3) │ 5              │ 184             │                                              
├─────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┼─────────────────┤                                              
│ Mean speed, 2000–3600 m             │ about 127 km/h │ about 100 km/h  │                                              
└─────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────┴─────────────────┘                                              
                                                                                                                        
- Confirmed: the table is wrong. Measured km/h per 1000 rpm are:                                                        
    - gear 2: 8.78                                                                                                      
    - gear 3: 10.85                                                                                                     
    - gear 4: 12.96                                                                                                     
    - gear 5: 14.56                                                                                                     
    - gear 6: 15.89                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                        
  The old table was 1.7–2.8× too high. Gear 1 can't be measured because the car is only in it at the standing start.    
  Your "about 17" for 6th is close to the measured 15.9.                                                                
                                                                                                                        
- Confirmed: replaying the old rule on each downshift tick reproduces the observed target gear in 115 of 115 downshifts.
  Almost all of them fired at brake ≤ 0.3, and most dropped two or more gears.                                          
                                                                                                                        
- Refuted as the sole cause of the 13 s: the fast run has the same bug, with 58 downshifts. Gear changes before 2000 m  
  are also about equal (88 vs 86).                                                                                      
                                                                                                                        
- Where the loss shows up: after 2000 m the repeat has a steering oscillation, with 184 sign flips against 5 and much   
  higher mean |steer|.                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                        
- Not tied to gear changes: at about 2260–2310 m the repeat oscillates in 6th with no gear change for roughly 70 ticks. 
  So the gear hunting aggravates the problem, but the steering loop is the likelier root cause.                         
                                                                                                                        
2. Fix in src/torcs_v3_physics.py                                                                                       
- _GEAR_SPEED_KMH_PER_1000RPM now holds the measured values.                                                            
- shift_gears(S, current_gear, brake=0.0) now takes the brake value instead of a braking flag. It downshifts one gear   
  only when brake > 0.5, rpm is below the new GEAR_DOWN_RPM_BRAKE (5500), and the resulting rpm would not exceed        
  GEAR_UP_RPM.                                                                                                          
- The braking downshift never targets gear 1, and GEAR_HOLD_TICKS still applies.                                        
- No other parameter changed, and src/torcs_v3_FINAL.py is untouched.                                                   
                                                                                                                        
3. Self-test: python src/torcs_v3_physics.py --selftest passes all 10 checks. The new ones are:                         
- 100 km/h in 6th at brake 0.3 stays at gear 5 or higher.                                                               
- Hard braking at low rpm drops exactly one gear.                                                                       
- A downshift that would push rpm above GEAR_UP_RPM is refused.                                                         
                                                                                                                        
4. CHANGELOG.md: the V3.9 entry holds the comparison table, the measured ratios, the verdict and the changes. It says   
V3.9 hasn't been raced.                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                        
If a repeat run of V3.9 still shows more than about 20 steering sign flips per lap, look at the steering aim and        
centering loop next.                                                                                                    
